CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:First Thursdays showcase the diversity of arts and humanities a
 t IU Bloomington and offer a welcoming environment for students\, faculty\
 , staff\, and community members to explore new creative outlets. Each even
 t is a unique opportunity to experience the wonderful work of artists\, pe
 rformers\, and scholars from all across campus and around town.\nThe April
  First Thursdays will be a festival of art\, ideas\, and community featuri
 ng 2 performance stages\, 80+ activity booths\, 20+ arts vendors\, food tr
 ucks\, giveaways\, and more. Around the IU Fine Arts Plaza\, there will be
  a 1776 Trail\, poster printing\, 3D fabrication demos\, and henna tattooi
 ng among many other activities. On the main stage\, we’ll have performance
 s by Soul Revue\, Eleanor & Dario\, Jacobs Saxophone Ensemble\, IU Musical
  Theatre\, and InMotion Dance Company. For more details\, visit  go.iu.edu
 /first-thursdays.\n 
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260402T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260402T190000
LOCATION:IU Fine Arts Plaza\, 1201 E 7th St\, Bloomington
