X-SOURCE-URLS:{"IU Hamilton Lugar School": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2209440-meet-the-barbarians-film-screening", "IU Bloomington Libraries": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2209440-meet-the-barbarians-film-screening"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"IU Hamilton Lugar School": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2209440-meet-the-barbarians-film-screening"}
X-SOURCE-ID:iu_hamilton_lugar
X-SOURCE:IU Bloomington Libraries, IU Hamilton Lugar School
DTSTART:20260402T210000Z
DTEND:20260402T220000Z
LOCATION:HERMAN B WELLS LIBRARY - Room Number: Screening Room
GEO:39.171003;-86.516793
SUMMARY:"Meet the Barbarians" Film Screening
DESCRIPTION:Join us at the Wells Library screening room to watch French f
 ilm Meet the Barbarians\, part of the HLS Movie Night series.  When a Fre
 nch village accidentally welcomes the "wrong" refugee family\, their assu
 mptions get turned upside down. Director Julie Delpy's warm\, funny drame
 dy asks who the real barbarians are when fear meets humanity.  This film 
 was the summer 2024 box office hit in Europe. The town council of Paimpon
 t\, a small village in Brittany\, has unanimously voted in favor of welco
 ming a family of Ukrainian refugees. However\, the refugees who turn up a
 ren't Ukrainian but Syrian\, and some of the locals are not very pleased 
 with their new neighbors. Yet the Fayad family avoids all the clichés th
 e French villagers may have expected. So much so that\, they leave one wo
 ndering: who in this little village are the true 'barbarians'? A film tha
 t gives you laughs\, tears\, cheers\, and a good dose of Breton Sun.&#160
 \;  Watch a trailer for the film here. (https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6
 MBI076ZRU8)
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Join us at the Wells Library screening 
 room to watch French film <em data-start="114" data-end="137">Meet the Ba
 rbarians\,</em> part of the HLS Movie Night series.</p><p>  When a French
  village accidentally welcomes the "wrong" refugee family\, their assumpt
 ions get turned upside down. Director Julie Delpy's warm\, funny dramedy 
 asks who the real barbarians are when fear meets humanity.</p><p>  This f
 ilm was the summer 2024 box office hit in Europe. The town council of Pai
 mpont\, a small village in Brittany\, has unanimously voted in favor of w
 elcoming a family of Ukrainian refugees. However\, the refugees who turn 
 up aren't Ukrainian but Syrian\, and some of the locals are not very plea
 sed with their new neighbors. Yet the Fayad family avoids all the cliché
 s the French villagers may have expected. So much so that\, they leave on
 e wondering: who in this little village are the true 'barbarians'? A film
  that gives you laughs\, tears\, cheers\, and a good dose of Breton Sun.&
 #160\;</p><p>  Watch a trailer for the film <a href="https://www.youtube.
 com/watch?v=6MBI076ZRU8">here.</a></p>
UID:20260402T210000Z-2209447@events.iu.edu
DTSTAMP:20260213T142045Z
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2209440-meet-the-barbarians-film-sc
 reening
