SUMMARY:Latino Studies Undergraduate Research Symposium
DESCRIPTION:Held biannually\, the Latino Studies Undergraduate Research S
 ymposium allows students to conduct research focusing on Latinxs in the U
 .S. and in transnational contexts. Undergraduate students undertake a sus
 tained research project of their choosing\, culminating in a two-day symp
 osium to showcase their research. The Symposium bridges undergraduate\, g
 raduate\, and faculty research by partnering each undergraduate participa
 nt with a mentor who helps plan and directs the research.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Held biannually\, the Latino Studies Un
 dergraduate Research Symposium allows students to conduct research focusi
 ng on Latinxs in the U.S. and in transnational contexts. Undergraduate st
 udents undertake a sustained research project of their choosing\, culmina
 ting in a two-day symposium to showcase their research. The Symposium bri
 dges undergraduate\, graduate\, and faculty research by partnering each u
 ndergraduate participant with a mentor who helps plan and directs the res
 earch.</p>
