SUMMARY:April Gallery Walk | Opening Reception + Book Signing with Rania M
 atar
DTSTART;TZID=EDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260403T170000
DTEND;TZID=EDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260403T200000
UID:2603263v0dj2XKkUyCsN1sx8XozA
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://citysparkstorage.blob.core.windows.net/p
 ortalimages/portalimages/6ykcbf6dgkSTuuDSRt7bZg.large.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a Gallery Walk Opening Reception with exhibiting p
 hotographer\, Rania Matar. We will open the exhibition with a reading from
  janan alexandra. Both Rania and janan will have books available to sign 
 during the opening.\n\nPictura Gallery is pleased to present Rania Matar
 ’s series\, SHE هي\, which looks at young women coming of age in th
 e US and in Lebanon. Matar is a Lebanese-born\, American/Palestinian artis
 t. She has dedicated her work to exploring issues of personal and collecti
 ve identity\, through photographs of female adolescence and womanhood. Mat
 ar’s portraits capture the lives of young women who persist in uncertain
  times.\n\nThe Sidney and Lois Eskenazi Museum of Art is currently exhibit
 ing another one of Matar's series\, Where Do I Go? لوين روح؟. It 
 is on view March 5 - August 9 in the Rhonda and Anthony Moravec Gallery\, 
 Center for Prints\, Drawings\, and Photographs\, Third Floor.
LOCATION:Pictura Gallery
URL:https://www.thefar.org/events/event/116262/
X-SOURCE:CitySpark Bloomington
END:VEVENT
