X-SOURCE-URLS:{"WFHB Community Calendar": "https://wfhb.org/event/author-event-with-randal-m-jelks/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:wfhb
X-SOURCE:WFHB Community Calendar
UID:ai1ec-147837@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260401T021218Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Author and IU professor Randal Maurice Jelks celebrates the rel
 ease of his new book\, My America: Langston Hughes on Democracy.\nABOUT TH
 E BOOK:\nMy America traces Hughes’s journey from a child captivated by the
  wonder of Kansas City to cosmopolitan witness in Paris\, New York\, Mexic
 o City\, and Madrid. Langston Hughes is one of the few American writers wh
 o consistently wrote about democracy from a joyous perspective\, and My Am
 erica explores how his works speak to the political anxieties and crises w
 e face today.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260407T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260407T190000
LOCATION:Morgenstern Books & Cafe\, 849 South Auto Mall Road\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Author Event with Randal M. Jelks
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/author-event-with-randal-m-jelks/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p dir='ltr'>Aut
 hor and IU professor Randal Maurice Jelks celebrates the release of his ne
 w book\, <em>My America: Langston Hughes on Democracy.</em></p>\n<p dir='l
 tr'>ABOUT THE BOOK:</p>\n<p dir='ltr'>My America traces Hughes’s journey f
 rom a child captivated by the wonder of Kansas City to cosmopolitan witnes
 s in Paris\, New York\, Mexico City\, and Madrid. Langston Hughes is one o
 f the few American writers who consistently wrote about democracy from a j
 oyous perspective\, and My America explores how his works speak to the pol
 itical anxieties and crises we face today.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
