SUMMARY: The Shadow Scholars w/ filmmaker | In Light Human Rights Documen
 tary Film Festival
DESCRIPTION:In The Shadow Scholars\, Oxford's youngest Black professor\, 
 Patricia Kingori\, delves into a multibillion-dollar underground industry
  where 40\,000 educated Kenyans ghostwrite essays for students often in A
 merican\, British\, or Australian institutions. Filmed across three conti
 nents amid crackdowns and AI threats\, it probes into the colonization of
  knowledge\, racial inequities\, and the exploitation of African labor. [
 97 min\; documentary\; English]\n\nA Q&A with filmmaker Eloïse King and K
 elsey Grimm (Curator of Archives and Library Resources\, IU Museum of Arc
 haeology and Anthropology) will follow the screening.
CATEGORIES:Free
X-TKF-FEATURED-IMAGE:https://d3flpus5evl89n.cloudfront.net/62fb9509b27fd5
 06428328ed/69c455c6701bd67becad9db4/scaled_1024.jpg
