UID:c3ee5515-de61-4747-a441-35247a66584f@bloomington-online
CREATED:20260326T155429Z
DESCRIPTION:Eric Ries will discuss his new book "Incorruptible: Why Good Co
 mpanies Go Bad and How Great Companies Stay Great."\n\nThis in-store event 
 features Eric Ries joining virtually\, moderated by Erik Coyne\, Chancellor
  of Ivy Tech Bloomington.\n\nPartners: Ivy Tech Community College Gayle & B
 ill Cook Center for Entrepreneurship and the South Central Indiana Small Bu
 siness Development Center.\n\nNote: The book releases May 26\, 2026. Copies
  will not be available at the event — preorders available at Morgenstern Bo
 oks for in-store pickup or shipping.\n\nABOUT THE BOOK: From the creator of
  The Lean Startup comes a rethink of how organizations are built and why su
 ccess itself so often turns companies against their founding principles. In
 corruptible argues that corporate drift is structural\, not ethical. When g
 overnance systems are poorly designed\, even principled leaders are pushed 
 toward outcomes they never wanted. Ries offers a practical blueprint for bu
 ilding enduring\, mission-controlled companies.\n\nTickets / RSVP: https://
 www.eventbrite.com/e/eric-ries-on-incorruptible-tickets-1985310867247
LAST-MODIFIED:20260326T155430Z
LOCATION:Morgenstern Books & Café\, 849 S Auto Mall Rd\, Bloomington\, IN 4
 7401
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Author Event: Eric Ries — Incorruptible
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
